= Resolution to Extend DuFour's Term

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> seeks to amend the constitution to extend DuFour’s term by two years — keeping their strongman in office and sparing themselves a vote they might not control. But with a two-thirds majority required, they may need our votes to pull it off.

After witnessing DuFour try to appoint [+ chancellor +] of all people, why in hell would we lift a finger to help him? The choice is obvious.

- @oppose_resolution: We will vote against the resolution, insisting that an election be held in accordance with the constitution.

@oppose_resolution
go-to: hindenburg_extended if goerdeler_right_coalition + royalist_r >= 66.6; hindenburg_failed if goerdeler_right_coalition + royalist_r < 66.6

Of course, we will oppose this undemocratic act—the people should decide whether DuFour receives another term or not. 

@hindenburg_extended
on-arrival: dufour_term_extended = 1

Despite opposition from the <span style="color: #c00000;">left-wing</span> parties, the resolution passes with the support of all parties to our right[? if not lvp_formed:, except for the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if not unionist_in_gov_mini: and <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?]?][? if lvp_formed and not unionist_in_gov_mini: except for the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?].

@hindenburg_failed
on-arrival: dufour_term_extended = 0

We’ve successfully defeated the motion in the Assembly—elections will be held! The result has also sown dissent within the governing coalition.